-- title:
--   The compact orthogonal group $O(5)$, its Haar measure and one-parameter subgroups
-- statement:
--   Let $M_5(\mathbb{R})$ be the real $5\times5$ matrices and $O(5)=\{A:A^{\mathsf T}A=I\}$ the orthogonal group.
--
--   1. **Bounds and compactness.** Every row of an orthogonal matrix has squared length $1$, so all entries satisfy $|A_{ij}|\le1$. Hence $O(5)$, being closed, is compact.
--   2. **Haar measure.** $O(5)$ carries its Borel $\sigma$-algebra and the measure $\mu=(\text{Haar measure})^{-1}$, the image of a left Haar measure under inversion. It is finite, right-invariant, and gives positive mass to nonempty open sets.
--   3. **One-parameter subgroups.** For a skew-symmetric matrix $X$ ($X^{\mathsf T}=-X$) and $t\in\mathbb{R}$, $\exp(tX)\in O(5)$.
--
--   The Haar measure lets one average functions over the orthogonal group acting on the quadric. The one-parameter subgroups supply the infinitesimal rotations used in gradient-flow deformations.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `RM` is `Matrix (Fin 5) (Fin 5) ℝ` and `O5` is `Matrix.orthogonalGroup (Fin 5) ℝ`. A local instance makes the matrix transpose continuous for the operator-norm topology.
